{%- comment -%}
  App Embed Block — target: head. ONE block that owns the whole feature:
  pre-paint FOUC prevention, JSON data island, controller script and the
  custom-element placeholder. Shopify injects this just before </head>,
  so the inline <style>/<script>/<link>/JSON-island parts are parsed
  during <head> parsing — before the <body> / native gallery is painted,
  which is the only true pre-paint hook.

  How the HTML parser places things:
    Everything except <cp-embed-gallery> is head-valid (<style>, <script>,
    <link>) and stays in <head>. The <cp-embed-gallery> placeholder is
    NOT head-valid, so when the parser encounters it the head insertion
    mode ends implicitly (per HTML5 spec) and the element is placed as
    the FIRST <body> child. The deferred controller script (registered
    in head) then upgrades that placeholder and `connectedCallback`
    fires → _init resolves the native gallery, hides it per-element,
    releases the blanket class and mounts the custom gallery.

  FOUC flow:
    1. Setter script (synchronous, head-parse) reads the JSON data island
       above it and, ONLY if the current variant actually has images
       (resolved from ?variant= or product.selected_or_first_available_
       variant — [name="id"] does not exist yet at head-parse), adds
       `cp-vg-prehide` to <html>. The blanket <style> hides all default-
       selector native galleries pre-paint via visibility:hidden (layout
       reserved → no shift when revealed).
    2. window.__cpVgFouc.prehideTimer (3s) is the only fail-safe to drop
       the class if the controller never mounts.
    3. The deferred controller runs at DOMContentLoaded, _tick releases
       the blanket synchronously THEN applies the precise per-element
       .cp-vg-native-hidden hide in the same tick → no flash. On AJAX
       variant switch the controller re-adds the blanket synchronously
       (observer + event handlers gated by _needsCover) and releases on
       the next tick.

  Constraints (Shopify): app embed blocks have only Global Liquid scope
  (`product` is available on product pages). The bundled Shopify
  stylesheet tag is forbidden in app blocks — plain <style>/<script>
  only. Custom elements as direct head children are not head-valid, so
  the placeholder MUST be last in this block (or the parser closes head
  early and metadata after it ends up in body).
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- if product != blank -%}

{%- comment -%}
  R3-H1: `| json` escapes JSON syntax but NOT `<`, so an attacker-influenced
  variant.title containing `</script><script>…` would break out of this
  JSON island and inject script regardless of the JS-side _esc(). Every
  free-text value interpolated below MUST additionally neutralise `<`/`>`
  by replacing them with their \uXXXX JSON escapes (JSON.parse restores
  them, so data is unchanged). Image URLs are Shopify CDN and
  IDs/dimensions are numeric, so only variant.title needs this.
{%- endcomment -%}
<script type="application/json" id="cp-embed-data-{{ block.id }}">
  {
    {%- for variant in product.variants -%}
      {%- assign vg = variant.metafields.custom.variant_gallery -%}
      "{{ variant.id }}": [
        {%- assign cp_has_any = false -%}
        {%- comment -%} Step 1: if variant has variant_gallery metafield, prefer those images (restricted to this variant). featured_image as primary. {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- if vg != blank and vg.value != blank -%}
          {%- if variant.featured_image != blank -%}
            {%- assign vfi = variant.featured_image -%}
            {
              "type":     "image",
              "src_400":  {{ vfi | image_url: width: 400  | json }},
              "src_800":  {{ vfi | image_url: width: 800  | json }},
              "src_1200": {{ vfi | image_url: width: 1200 | json }},
              "thumb":    {{ vfi | image_url: width: 160  | json }},
              "w":        {{ vfi.width  | json }},
              "h":        {{ vfi.height | json }},
              "alt":      {{ variant.title | json | replace: "<", "\u003c" | replace: ">", "\u003e" }}
            }
            {%- assign cp_has_any = true -%}
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- comment -%} vg.value items via list.file_reference: dispatch on media_type so videos and 3D models added to the metafield are honoured, not silently dropped (previously this branch was image-only). {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- for item in vg.value -%}
            {%- if item.media_type == 'image' -%}
              {%- assign cp_src = item | image_url: width: 800 -%}
              {%- if cp_src != blank -%}
                {%- if cp_has_any %},{% endif -%}
                {%- assign cp_w = item.preview_image.width  | default: item.width -%}
                {%- assign cp_h = item.preview_image.height | default: item.height -%}
                {
                  "type":     "image",
                  "src_400":  {{ item | image_url: width: 400  | json }},
                  "src_800":  {{ cp_src | json }},
                  "src_1200": {{ item | image_url: width: 1200 | json }},
                  "thumb":    {{ item | image_url: width: 160  | json }},
                  "w":        {{ cp_w | json }},
                  "h":        {{ cp_h | json }},
                  "alt":      {{ item.alt | default: variant.title | json | replace: "<", "\u003c" | replace: ">", "\u003e" }}
                }
                {%- assign cp_has_any = true -%}
              {%- endif -%}
            {%- elsif item.media_type == 'video' -%}
              {%- if item.preview_image != blank -%}
                {%- if cp_has_any %},{% endif -%}
                {%- assign cp_pi = item.preview_image -%}
                {
                  "type":   "video",
                  "thumb":  {{ cp_pi | image_url: width: 160  | json }},
                  "poster": {{ cp_pi | image_url: width: 1200 | json }},
                  "w":      {{ cp_pi.width  | json }},
                  "h":      {{ cp_pi.height | json }},
                  "alt":    {{ item.alt | default: variant.title | json | replace: "<", "\u003c" | replace: ">", "\u003e" }},
                  "sources": [
                    {%- for src in item.sources -%}
                      {%- unless forloop.first %},{% endunless -%}
                      {"src": {{ src.url | json }}, "mime": {{ src.mime_type | json }}}
                    {%- endfor -%}
                  ]
                }
                {%- assign cp_has_any = true -%}
              {%- endif -%}
            {%- elsif item.media_type == 'model' -%}
              {%- if item.preview_image != blank -%}
                {%- assign cp_glb = blank -%}
                {%- for src in item.sources -%}
                  {%- if src.format == 'glb' and cp_glb == blank -%}{%- assign cp_glb = src.url -%}{%- endif -%}
                {%- endfor -%}
                {%- if cp_glb != blank -%}
                  {%- if cp_has_any %},{% endif -%}
                  {%- assign cp_pi = item.preview_image -%}
                  {
                    "type":      "model",
                    "thumb":     {{ cp_pi | image_url: width: 160  | json }},
                    "poster":    {{ cp_pi | image_url: width: 1200 | json }},
                    "w":         {{ cp_pi.width  | json }},
                    "h":         {{ cp_pi.height | json }},
                    "alt":       {{ item.alt | default: variant.title | json | replace: "<", "\u003c" | replace: ">", "\u003e" }},
                    "model_src": {{ cp_glb | json }}
                  }
                  {%- assign cp_has_any = true -%}
                {%- endif -%}
              {%- endif -%}
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- endfor -%}
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- comment -%} Step 2: if no images from metafield, fall back to product.media. Handles ALL media types so a merchant-uploaded video / 3D model is no longer silently dropped (Bilder + Video-Player). featured_image emitted first as primary (RISK-4) and deduped from the loop. {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- unless cp_has_any -%}
          {%- assign cp_vfi_id = blank -%}
          {%- if variant.featured_image != blank -%}
            {%- assign vfi = variant.featured_image -%}
            {
              "type":     "image",
              "src_400":  {{ vfi | image_url: width: 400  | json }},
              "src_800":  {{ vfi | image_url: width: 800  | json }},
              "src_1200": {{ vfi | image_url: width: 1200 | json }},
              "thumb":    {{ vfi | image_url: width: 160  | json }},
              "w":        {{ vfi.width  | json }},
              "h":        {{ vfi.height | json }},
              "alt":      {{ variant.title | json | replace: "<", "\u003c" | replace: ">", "\u003e" }}
            }
            {%- assign cp_has_any = true -%}
            {%- assign cp_vfi_id = vfi.id -%}
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- for media in product.media -%}
            {%- if media.id != cp_vfi_id -%}
              {%- if media.media_type == 'image' -%}
                {%- assign cp_src = media | image_url: width: 800 -%}
                {%- if cp_src != blank -%}
                  {%- if cp_has_any %},{% endif -%}
                  {%- assign cp_w = media.preview_image.width  | default: media.width -%}
                  {%- assign cp_h = media.preview_image.height | default: media.height -%}
                  {
                    "type":     "image",
                    "src_400":  {{ media | image_url: width: 400  | json }},
                    "src_800":  {{ cp_src | json }},
                    "src_1200": {{ media | image_url: width: 1200 | json }},
                    "thumb":    {{ media | image_url: width: 160  | json }},
                    "w":        {{ cp_w | json }},
                    "h":        {{ cp_h | json }},
                    "alt":      {{ media.alt | default: product.title | json | replace: "<", "\u003c" | replace: ">", "\u003e" }}
                  }
                  {%- assign cp_has_any = true -%}
                {%- endif -%}
              {%- elsif media.media_type == 'video' -%}
                {%- if media.preview_image != blank -%}
                  {%- if cp_has_any %},{% endif -%}
                  {%- assign cp_pi = media.preview_image -%}
                  {
                    "type":   "video",
                    "thumb":  {{ cp_pi | image_url: width: 160  | json }},
                    "poster": {{ cp_pi | image_url: width: 1200 | json }},
                    "w":      {{ cp_pi.width  | json }},
                    "h":      {{ cp_pi.height | json }},
                    "alt":    {{ media.alt | default: product.title | json | replace: "<", "\u003c" | replace: ">", "\u003e" }},
                    "sources": [
                      {%- for src in media.sources -%}
                        {%- unless forloop.first %},{% endunless -%}
                        {"src": {{ src.url | json }}, "mime": {{ src.mime_type | json }}}
                      {%- endfor -%}
                    ]
                  }
                  {%- assign cp_has_any = true -%}
                {%- endif -%}
              {%- elsif media.media_type == 'external_video' -%}
                {%- if media.preview_image != blank -%}
                  {%- if cp_has_any %},{% endif -%}
                  {%- assign cp_pi = media.preview_image -%}
                  {
                    "type":        "external_video",
                    "thumb":       {{ cp_pi | image_url: width: 160  | json }},
                    "poster":      {{ cp_pi | image_url: width: 1200 | json }},
                    "w":           {{ cp_pi.width  | json }},
                    "h":           {{ cp_pi.height | json }},
                    "alt":         {{ media.alt | default: product.title | json | replace: "<", "\u003c" | replace: ">", "\u003e" }},
                    "host":        {{ media.host | json }},
                    "external_id": {{ media.external_id | json }}
                  }
                  {%- assign cp_has_any = true -%}
                {%- endif -%}
              {%- elsif media.media_type == 'model' -%}
                {%- if media.preview_image != blank -%}
                  {%- assign cp_glb = blank -%}
                  {%- for src in media.sources -%}
                    {%- if src.format == 'glb' and cp_glb == blank -%}{%- assign cp_glb = src.url -%}{%- endif -%}
                  {%- endfor -%}
                  {%- if cp_glb != blank -%}
                    {%- if cp_has_any %},{% endif -%}
                    {%- assign cp_pi = media.preview_image -%}
                    {
                      "type":      "model",
                      "thumb":     {{ cp_pi | image_url: width: 160  | json }},
                      "poster":    {{ cp_pi | image_url: width: 1200 | json }},
                      "w":         {{ cp_pi.width  | json }},
                      "h":         {{ cp_pi.height | json }},
                      "alt":       {{ media.alt | default: product.title | json | replace: "<", "\u003c" | replace: ">", "\u003e" }},
                      "model_src": {{ cp_glb | json }}
                    }
                    {%- assign cp_has_any = true -%}
                  {%- endif -%}
                {%- endif -%}
              {%- endif -%}
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- endfor -%}
        {%- endunless -%}
      ]{% unless forloop.last %},{% endunless %}
    {%- endfor -%}
  }
</script>

{%- comment -%}
  Pre-paint setter. Reads the JSON island above (single source of truth,
  no duplicated has-images logic), resolves the current variant from
  ?variant= or selected_or_first_available_variant (no [name="id"] in
  the DOM yet at head-parse time — the controller handles late
  corrections), and adds `cp-vg-prehide` to <html> ONLY if data[id] is
  non-empty. This is now perfectly aligned with the controller decision
  (a variant whose variant_gallery is set but whose every image_url is
  empty yields an empty data[id] and is NOT pre-hidden).

  Security: only numeric IDs and the canonical class literal are used —
  no merchant-controlled value is interpolated into JS strings here.
{%- endcomment -%}
<script>
  (function () {
    try {
      var el = document.getElementById('cp-embed-data-{{ block.id }}');
      if (!el) return;
      var data = JSON.parse(el.textContent);
      var id = null;
      try { id = new URL(window.location.href).searchParams.get('variant'); } catch (e) {}
      if (!id) id = {{ product.selected_or_first_available_variant.id | json }};
      if (id == null) return;
      var imgs = data[String(id)];
      if (!(imgs && imgs.length)) return;
      document.documentElement.classList.add('cp-vg-prehide');
      window.__cpVgFouc = window.__cpVgFouc || {};
      window.__cpVgFouc.prehideTimer = window.setTimeout(function () {
        document.documentElement.classList.remove('cp-vg-prehide');
      }, 3000);
    } catch (e) { /* never block page render */ }
  })();
</script>

{%- comment -%}
  CANONICAL native-selector list. Kept in sync with the _selectors array
  in assets/variant-gallery-embed.js — change both together.
  visibility:hidden reserves layout (no shift when the blanket is
  released and the controller's per-element display:none takes over).
{%- endcomment -%}
<style>
  html.cp-vg-prehide media-gallery,
  html.cp-vg-prehide [id^="MediaGallery"],
  html.cp-vg-prehide .product__media-wrapper,
  html.cp-vg-prehide .product__media-list { visibility: hidden !important; }
</style>

<style>.cp-vg-native-hidden{display:none !important;}</style>

{{ 'variant-gallery-embed.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
<script src="{{ 'variant-gallery-embed.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>

{%- comment -%}
  Placeholder element. NOT head-valid per HTML5, so the parser closes
  <head> implicitly when it reaches this tag and places the element as
  the first <body> child. Everything above (head-valid) therefore stays
  in <head> and is parsed pre-paint. Keep this LAST inside the if-block
  for that invariant to hold.
{%- endcomment -%}
<cp-embed-gallery
  id="cp-embed-gallery-{{ block.id }}"
  class="cp-embed-gallery"
  style="--cp-thumb-size: {{ block.settings.thumbnail_size }}px; display: none;"
  data-block-id="{{ block.id }}"
  data-native-selector="{{ block.settings.native_gallery_selector }}"
  data-scope-selector="{{ block.settings.scope_selector }}"
  data-extra-hide="{{ block.settings.extra_hide_selector }}"
  data-thumb-size="{{ block.settings.thumbnail_size }}"
  data-show-thumbs="{% if block.settings.enable_thumbnails %}1{% endif %}"
  data-thumb-pos="{{ block.settings.thumbnail_position | default: 'bottom' }}"
>
  <div class="cp-gallery__inner"></div>
</cp-embed-gallery>

{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Variant Image Gallery",
  "target": "head",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "enable_thumbnails",
      "label": "Show thumbnails",
      "default": false,
      "info": "Off: all relevant images stack vertically at full width (matches a typical Shopify gallery). On: a single main image is shown with a clickable thumbnail strip in the position chosen below."
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "thumbnail_position",
      "label": "Thumbnail position",
      "default": "bottom",
      "options": [
        { "value": "bottom", "label": "Below main image" },
        { "value": "top", "label": "Above main image" },
        { "value": "left", "label": "Left of main image" },
        { "value": "right", "label": "Right of main image" }
      ],
      "info": "Only applies when 'Show thumbnails' is enabled. Long lists scroll horizontally (top/bottom) or vertically (left/right) with arrow controls on hover."
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "thumbnail_size",
      "label": "Thumbnail size (px)",
      "min": 60,
      "max": 200,
      "step": 10,
      "default": 80
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "native_gallery_selector",
      "label": "Native gallery CSS selector",
      "default": "media-gallery",
      "info": "CSS selector of your theme's native product image gallery. Default works for Dawn theme. For other themes inspect the gallery element and enter its tag or class (e.g. .product__media-wrapper)."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "scope_selector",
      "label": "Product container selector (optional)",
      "info": "Restricts the native gallery search to this container so quick-view / modal galleries elsewhere on the page are not matched. Leave empty for the whole page."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "extra_hide_selector",
      "label": "Extra elements to hide (optional)",
      "info": "Comma-separated CSS selectors for separate native thumbnail / zoom elements some themes render outside the gallery. Leave empty unless leftover native thumbnails appear."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Automatically replaces the native product gallery with variant-specific images from ContentPilot AI. Enable this embed once — no block placement needed."
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
